--- result — constructors for the Result type (ADR-0077).
---
--- The result library provides `result.ok` and `result.err`, the
--- constructors for the `Result` type. They are pure handl arrows built
--- on the nominal tag system (ADR-0055): an `Ok` result is a tagged value
--- `{"__tag__": "ok", "value": <T>}` and an `Err` result is
--- `{"__tag__": "err", "value": <E>}`.
---
--- Predicates (`is_ok`, `is_err`) are not provided — use `mood.int(r, ok)`
--- and `mood.int(r, err)` directly, or pattern match with
--- `match r { ok(v) => ..., err(e) => ... }`.

--- result.ok — construct an Ok result wrapping a value.
--- The value is tagged with the `ok` nominal tag (ADR-0055/0077).
--- Contract: IsOk(output)
tag ok = Value

--- result.err — construct an Err result wrapping an error.
--- The error is tagged with the `err` nominal tag (ADR-0055/0077).
--- Contract: IsErr(output)
tag err = Error

{
  ok: ok,
  err: err,
}
